+Use case: compositing / precise-object-edit. Edit the supplied background.png, the exact website hero base, into a premium photoreal daylight science-fiction hero, target canvas 2880 x 1800 (8:5). Preserve the entire blue sky gradient, soft clouds, and existing navigation unchanged. Add ONE immense engineered neural-network tree limb entering from OFFSCREEN RIGHT. No ground, trunk base, roots or standalone tree. The branch IS a structured neural network designed for later SVG backpropagation animation, shown at REST.
+
+CRITICAL COMPOSITION, coordinates measured on the 2880x1800 canvas: main input limb crosses the right edge with centre y=520 and thickness 430 pixels, tapering inward to first hub around (2500,650). Body fills right half only. It divides LEFTWARD in FOUR readable, discrete tiers and fans wider toward the LEFT, canopy seen slightly from below. First round glass/metal neuron hub 130px across at (2470,650) splits into exactly THREE gently curved structural limbs to three round hubs around x=2180 at y=440,740,1040. Each of those splits leftward into THREE thinner limbs with round hubs near x=1800. Each of those splits into FOUR fine smooth branches, with small round junctions and tiny terminal output buds near x=1300-1500. Uppermost fine tips may reach x=1180 if y<650. Spread terminals between y=310 and y=1150, keeping every element at y>=700 to the RIGHT of x=1270. Every fork MUST have a clearly visible round node physically integrated into it. These are branching solid limbs, not bundles of separate wires. Thickness approximately constant between each tier of nodes, with progressive reductions at forks. Show discrete tiers with open sky between limbs so one can visually trace paths from right input to left outputs. Add sparse very fine taut cross-connection threads between neighbouring tiers, not a messy web.
+
+MATERIAL: dark deep navy graphite #0b1a2b / gunmetal and carbon-fibre bark, organic grown curves fused with smooth machined surfaces, restrained brushed-metal joint rings and translucent glass/resin sections. No moss or green ivy. Every structural branch has ONE continuous, clean inset glass-core channel running visibly along its CAMERA-FACING centre from node to node, width 12-20 percent of limb thickness, even and unbroken. Channel is DARK blue-grey at rest with only a very faint pale cyan inner edge. Spherical nodes are smoked glass with a dim thin cyan ring, NOT luminous lamps. Keep emission extremely subdued: bright daylight reflections illuminate materials, not neon. Only tiny terminal buds may be bright. A maximum of two tiny warm orange details.
+
+FOLIAGE: a few small clusters of thin frosted-glass leaf plates near terminal tips only, never hiding forks or channels. A few fine hanging optical fibres/cables drop vertically on right half, longest reaching y=1450-1550. No loose objects. LIGHT: bright sun from upper right, sky reflections, top rim light, realistic complex dark material detail, slightly hazy far tips, subtle depth of field on closest right edge. High-end photoreal product-render / sci-fi film quality, NOT diagram illustration, not cartoon, no HUD, floating pixels, random glowing dots, or bright neon network.
+
+EXACT KEEP-OUT: entire y<230 remains original background/navigation; x<1250,y>=700 remains pure original sky; meeting pill stays entirely untouched. Do not add any text, labels, numbers, logos or watermarks. Keep sky dominant. Preserve v2-scale huge suspended canopy occupying approximately x1300-2880, y300-1550 while making the topology and traceable dim channels the most important feature.
+
+Image 1 is always the edit target, untouched base sky/navigation. Image 2 is the accepted reference build: preserve its photoreal carbon material, mostly dark unlit centre-line grooves, and FOUR-TIER topology with three first branches, three second branches per first branch, four fine twigs per secondary. Retain its 245px-thick input at the right edge and compact first round hub only 70px across, measured at the 1586px-wide reference scale. Later nodes smaller. The entire branch should remain in the right half after compositing; the raw candidate may follow reference placement. Avoid huge bulbs; highlights are daylight reflections not emitted light. Alter only what the variation calls for, while giving its silhouette a recognisable difference. Show central dark channel glass distinctly on camera-facing surface of EVERY branch. Do not replace structural channels with mere glowing edge outlines.
+
+02 WIDER AND DENSER: broaden the leftward fan, more layer-3 and layer-4 branches and terminals, more fine taut inter-layer threads. Dense yet organised with every fork and each individual central channel still readable. Keep three clear primary branches.
+Keep exact three large first branches, but make each next tier fan to FOUR rather than three, each splitting to four finer output tips. Add delicate straight taut cross-connections between layers. Dense, not tangled; no drooping loops connecting layers. Prefer a broader canopy with slightly irregular living curves and short staggered terminal ends.
